# Google Drive sync. Optional — with this unset the whole sync panel hides
# itself and the app is exactly what it was before: local-only, no account, no
# network. Set it and Settings grows a "Google Drive sync" panel.
#
# The client ID is PUBLIC by design. Google's browser token flow has no client
# secret at all: the only thing that stops another site using this ID is the
# list of Authorized JavaScript origins on the OAuth client itself. So this
# value is safe in a repo, in a bundle, and in a Vercel environment variable —
# and there is nothing here to rotate or leak.
#
# BOTH SETUP STEPS ARE DONE, and they are recorded here because a new client
# would need them again:
#
#   1. The client's Authorized JavaScript origins are http://localhost:5173,
#      http://localhost:4173, https://read.flyleaf.cc and
#      https://flyleaf-ereader.vercel.app. Google refuses the token request
#      with `origin_mismatch` from anywhere not on that list. If Connect ever
#      fails naming an origin, this list is why.
#   2. VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID is set for production, preview and development.
#      It is a build-time import.meta.env value, so changing it needs a fresh
#      deploy — an env edit alone does nothing.
#
# The scopes the app asks for are drive.appdata — a hidden folder the reader
# never sees in their Drive — and userinfo.email, only so the panel can say
# which account it is syncing to. Both are registered on the consent screen.
#
# THIS IS THIS APP'S OWN CLIENT, in its own Google Cloud project
# (`flyleaf-ereader`), with its own consent screen that says "Flyleaf eReader".
# It used to be Press's client, and that was wrong for two reasons the owner
# named: the consent screen is per-project, so a reader of THIS app was asked
# to trust "Flyleaf Press"; and `appDataFolder` is scoped to the CLIENT, so one
# hidden folder held both apps' backups and each app's delete had to filter on
# a tag to avoid taking the other's. Separate clients means separate folders and
# there is nothing left to get wrong. See SPEC.md § 15.1.
#
# The consent screen is in Testing with the owner as its one test user, which is
# the normal state for an unverified External app: only listed test users can
# connect. Publishing is a Google review, not a switch.
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=1093925806507-geheiusfcb8belpi6bdpl6p8afi74g99.apps.googleusercontent.com
